**average(nums)**

Write `average(nums)` using `reduce`: the mean of the numbers, or 0 for an empty array.

```js
function average(nums) {
  // TODO
  return 0;
}
```

back:
// Why: reduce without a starting value throws on an empty array, and 0 / 0 is NaN, so an
// empty array needs its own answer.
// Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/reduce
function average(nums) {
  if (nums.length === 0) return 0;
  const total = nums.reduce((sum, n) => sum + n, 0);
  return total / nums.length;
}

