**Fix doubled(nums)**

`doubled(nums)` should return a new array with every number doubled, but it returns `undefined`. Fix it.

```js
function doubled(nums) {
  return nums.forEach((n) => n * 2);
}
```

back:
// Why: forEach runs the callback for its side effects and always returns undefined. To
// build a new array from the results, use map.
// Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/forEach
function doubled(nums) {
  return nums.map((n) => n * 2);
}

